8,Anna Lewington Collection of Matsigenka and Yine Recordings,https://cla.berkeley.edu/collections/matsigenka_yine.html,"The recordings were made in the ... and Yine people (whose voices, to my knowledge, have not been recorded elsewhere), and include stories, songs, and flute and drum music....",Matsigenka,Maipurean
9,Matsigenka | Encyclopedia.com,https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/matsigenka-0,"The Matsigenka like to sing and are good at it. Their songs are hypnotic repetitions and counterpoint, performed in groups of up to four people and accompanied by musical instruments. A traditional instrument is a two-headed, monkey-skin drum. They also play flutes and panpipes.",Matsigenka,Maipurean
